  "overlap_measure": {
    "primary": "interval_jaccard",
    "interval_jaccard_definition": "For two burst sets on the same event, J = (total seconds covered by the intersection of their unions) / (total seconds covered by the union of their unions). Empty-vs-empty is defined as J = 1.0; empty-vs-nonempty is J = 0.0. Both counts reported.",
    "secondary": "burst_count_agreement",
    "burst_count_agreement_definition": "|k_1 - k_2| and the indicator k_1 == k_2, per event.",
    "why_primary": "The downstream use of this phase is burst-relative ANCHORING \u2014 every later horizon is measured from a burst boundary. What matters is therefore whether the same regions of the session get labeled, which is what interval overlap measures. Burst-count agreement can be perfect while the intervals sit in entirely different places, and can be poor while the same region is labeled with one extra split. Count agreement is reported alongside because it is the quantity a reader of chart 01 will compare, but it is not the failure-row-3 statistic."
  },
